  "body": "## What changed\n\nCapture the model without toolpaths and each operation separately.\nKeep the same camera for each case.\nUse stable filenames in catalog/<family>/<case>/.\nCollect all case PNG files and publish the images branch to origin without force.\nStage the blank and operation images for PDF generation in stable filename order.\nLink the seed gallery from its README and the catalog documentation.\nRecord the decision in docs/decisions/2858-catalog-operation-images.md.\n\nThe fork's catalog-screenshots branch holds 24 PNG files for five cases.\nNo PNG file is in this PR.\n\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: yes\n\n## Cause\n\nThe renderer captured all toolpaths in one image.\nThe collector accepted only one filename for each case.\nThe command committed the images locally but did not publish the branch.\n\n## Tests\n\n- catalog_screenshots_resolves_new_relative_outside_directory failed before the fix and passes after it.\n- catalog_capture_starts_blank_and_selects_one_operation failed before the fix and passes after it.\n- Restoring the old collector made the collection pin fail. Restoring the fix made it pass.\n- Removing publication made the remote branch assertion fail. Restoring the fix made it pass.\n- Restoring the old UI capture behavior made the selection pin fail. Restoring the fix made it pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed on `2b31dd853940c73768c767b65ee17db663d69a03`: three steps, zero failures.\n- The gate passed five app catalog tests, two UI catalog tests, 207 xtask unit tests, and 23 xtask integration tests.\n- The UI renderer test remains ignored in the default suite. Its explicit screenshot run passed.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p xtask -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed on `2b31dd853940c73768c767b65ee17db663d69a03`.\n- Two full screenshot runs passed with CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU=1 on Vulkan llvmpipe.\n- Both runs produced the same paths and the same image tree, c5f31157485efb2ab573b763ad419430ff0ba933.\n- The local images commit and origin/catalog-screenshots both identify afa273df91349a02159458301c1ef626da430ae3.\n- Visual inspection confirmed separate blank, face, pocket, and drill views for the seed case.\n\n- `catalog_screenshots_pdf_stages_blank_and_operation_images` checks the combined `catalog --screenshots --pdf` command.\n- The test checks each Markdown reference, the copied image bytes, stable order, and the PDF output.\n- Restoring the old PDF consumer failed with `missing PDF image (<0-blank.png>)`. Restoring the fix passed.\n- The review image link check failed on the original body. It passed with the five published PNG links below.\n\n## Review screenshots\n\nThe before image uses the predecessor renderer and the unchanged seed project.\nThe after images come from the published catalog captures at `afa273df91349a02159458301c1ef626da430ae3`.\nThe camera stays the same. The before image combines all toolpaths.\nThe after images show the blank model and one operation at a time.\nAll five review PNG files are on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n![Before: all toolpaths](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/888016d4bd31c319cae6e39d66080fd3953e2991/pr-2967/before-all-toolpaths.png)\n\n![After: blank model](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/888016d4bd31c319cae6e39d66080fd3953e2991/pr-2967/after-0-blank.png)\n\n![After: face operation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/888016d4bd31c319cae6e39d66080fd3953e2991/pr-2967/after-1-Face1.png)\n\n![After: pocket operation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/888016d4bd31c319cae6e39d66080fd3953e2991/pr-2967/after-2-2D-Pocket1.png)\n\n![After: drill operation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/888016d4bd31c319cae6e39d66080fd3953e2991/pr-2967/after-3-Drill1.png)\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff contains no changed .nc or .cl files.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nHardware GPU rendering was not exercised. The software Vulkan adapter rendered all images.\nThe combined PDF test uses local renderer, pandoc, and Chrome substitutes. It checks staging and command wiring.\nA real browser PDF render was not exercised for this review fix.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changed the selected files at the overlap check.\n\nChangelog: Catalog screenshots now show each operation and publish to an images-only branch.\n\nFixes #2858\n\n",
